  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Cefamandole may be associated with Streptococcal Infection through a chain of indications involving Cefoxitin and Cefonicid. Cefamandole is indicated for Peritonitis, Escherichia Coli Infection, and Urinary Tract Infection, all of which are linked to Cefoxitin and Cefonicid, respectively. These antibiotics are indicated for Streptococcal Infection, indicating a potential pathway where Cefamandole could be considered for treating infections caused by Streptococcus species. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of support for this relationship, with varying degrees of confidence across different disease types. The evidence highlights a mechanistic link between Cefamandole and Streptococcal Infection through its interactions with other antibiotics, but the strength of this relationship is not uniformly consistent across all disease categories.",
